The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (ret) {
    fwnode_handle_put(child);
    return ret;
}
Reason:
`devm_add_action_or_reset()` already invokes the cleanup action (`cs42l43_fwnode_put`) on failure, so an explicit `fwnode_handle_put(child)` inside the error path causes a double release of the fwnode reference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret)
    return ret;
Reason:
Removing the explicit `fwnode_handle_put(child)` call ensures that the fwnode is released only once by `cs42l43_fwnode_put` (invoked automatically by `devm_add_action_or_reset` on failure), preventing the double-put.

